# LF everywhere. This is not cosmetic:
#   - api-manager.sh shipped with CRLF and could NEVER execute; every
#     invocation died at the shebang with "/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such
#     file or directory". The API had never started. See issue #75.
#   - CRLF in .gitignore can break pattern matching on some git versions.
#   - CRLF in requirements.txt can confuse pip.
#
# A .gitattributes nobody verifies is a wish, so CI enforces this too.

# Default: normalise every text file git detects.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, for the ones where it actually breaks something.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
*.example       text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.gz            binary
*.tar           binary
*.pdf           binary
